    "15_2009_L": "Bill No. 15-F of 2009\nTHE  APPROPRIATION BILL, 2009\n   (AS PASSED BY THE HOUSES OF PARLIAMENT—\nLOK SABHA ON THE 24TH FEBRUARY, 2009\nRAJYA SABHA  ON THE 25TH FEBRUARY, 2009)\nASSENTED TO\nON 3 MARCH, 2009\nACT NO. 17 OF 2009\n\n1\nTHE APPROPRIATION BILL, 2009\nA\nBILL\nto authorise payment and appropriation of certain further sums from and out of the\nConsolidated Fund of India for the services of the financial year 2008-09.\nBE it enacted by Parliament in the Sixtieth Year of the Republic of India as follows:—\n1. This Act may be called the Appropriation Act, 2009.\n2. From and out of the Consolidated Fund of India there may be paid and applied sums\nnot exceeding those specified in column 3 of the Schedule amounting in the aggregate to the\nsum of four lakh seventy-one thousand seven hundred eighteen crores and fifty-three lakh\nrupees towards defraying the several charges which will come in the course of payment\nduring the financial year 2008-09 in respect of the services specified in column 2 of the\nSchedule.\n3. The sums authorised to be paid and applied from and out of the Consolidated Fund\nof India by this Act shall be appropriated for the services and purposes expressed in the\nSchedule in relation to the said year.\nShort title.\nAppropriation.\nIssue of\nRs.\n471718,53,00,000\nout of the\nConsolidated\nFund of India\nfor the financial\nyear 2008-09.\nBill No. 15-F of 2009\n\n1 Department of Agriculture and Cooperation ....................... Revenue 3,00,000 .. 3,00,000\n2 Department of Agricultural Research and Education .......... Revenue 89,21,00,000 .. 89,21,00,000\n3 Department of Animal Husbandry, Dairying and Fisheries Revenue 3,00,000 .. 3,00,000\n6 Department of Chemicals and Petrochemicals ................... Revenue 1,00,000 .. 1,00,000\n8 Ministry of Civil Aviation ...................................................... Revenue 206,99,00,000 .. 206,99,00,000\n10 Department of Commerce .....................................